From: ane-stack
Subject: [PATCH 0006] milc: machine-readable --json diagnostics for check/run/plan

Stacking: apply after 0001, 0002, 0003, 0004, 0005.

Agents need to assert on milc failures structurally instead of grepping stderr.
A top-level `--json` flag (or MILC_JSON=1) makes a supported subcommand emit its
result as a single JSON envelope on stdout, errors included:

  {"ok":false,"command":"run","error":{"stage":"io","code":null,
   "message":"...","path":"..."}}

check reports {"ok":bool,"path":...,"errors":[...],"warnings":[...]}; run emits a
success envelope with path/units/steps and per-step plus aggregate latency_ns;
plan keeps its existing op-table success output and gains the same error
envelope. The flag is stripped before subcommand arg parsers run, so it is
accepted anywhere on the command line, and `milc plan --json` (which owned the
flag for its op-table output) is unchanged. Human eprintln output is untouched
and goes to stderr, so `2>/dev/null` yields clean parseable stdout.

Adds a Diag type, envelope emitters, and minimal JSON escaping (no serde). Four
new run_cli tests assert parseable envelopes for failing check/run/plan and that
MILC_JSON=1 is honoured.

